  "narrative": "The independent validation for H14 arrives and strongly supports the MSI-high/WRN association across the full lung panel. Signed to the hypothesis direction, discovery R14 gives +0.790 (95% CI +0.760 to +0.819), and validation R26 gives +0.7896 (independent 0.384% validation interval +0.7364 to +0.8429). The two estimates are nearly identical and far exceed the approximate 10% relative-difference benchmark for a dependency outcome with WRN mean around -0.30. I therefore accept H14 as a validated dataset association: among lung CRISPR-screened lines, MSI-high lines show much more negative WRN dependency scores, i.e. stronger WRN dependency. This remains an association in the supplied dataset, not evidence of causal synthetic lethality or external generalizability beyond these lung lines. It also aligns with H7 in the adenocarcinoma-restricted population. The previously accepted SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency and KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency associations remain central supported findings. For H2, H3, and H4, I reopen them as active investigations with refined eligibility because pathway co-drivers may mask driver-specific dependencies: BRAF V600E dependency after excluding KRAS mutation and EGFR amplification, EGFR amplification dependency after excluding KRAS mutation and BRAF V600E, and ERBB2 amplification dependency after excluding KRAS mutation, EGFR amplification, and BRAF V600E. H24 becomes active with an all-lung MTAP-loss versus WRN test to improve precision over the adenocarcinoma-restricted null/uncertain result. I also test whether TP53 loss modifies the large SMARCA4-loss effect on SMARCA2 dependency. Existing active research-marker and QC checks should continue as negative-control/benchmark analyses. H20/H21 remain unresolved/deferred because their intervals do not convincingly show lineage interactions but are wide enough to allow modest effects.",
  "research_notes": "Validated accepted dataset associations: MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency across all lung (H14), especially adenocarcinoma (H7). KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency across lung and validated in adeno (H17/H13; H8 stronger-direction claim rejected/closed). SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency across lung (H15) and key subsets (H6/H19/H22); no ARID1A-alone association in SMARCA4-intact adeno (H18). Rejected/negative or weak so far: H2/H4 rejected but now active as driver-purity refinements; H3 unresolved/active; H9/H10/H11/H12 low magnitude/uncertain; H16 interaction unresolved; H20/H21 lineage interactions unresolved but deferred. Active next batch: hidden driver dependencies among KRAS-WT and pathway-excluded adeno lines, all-lung MTAP-WRN, SMARCA4-SMARCA2 interaction by TP53 loss, plus already registered all-lung KRAS/EGFR/USP7 and research marker/QC negative controls. Maintain distinction between dataset associations and biological mechanism or generalizability."
